      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "At the very beginning of the essay we would like to give a short survey of the temporary results and questions of scientific research about psychopathological reactions after open heart surgery under extracorporeal circulation. Then the case report will show how the patient copes with the surgery 8 weeks before until about 5 weeks after. Within the case report and the following discussion, special attention will be payed to interaction between patient and doctors as well as cooperation between psychosomatic therapists and cardiologists. The essay is a contribution to the discussion of possibilities and limits of psychosomatic liaison services."},
